{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":832,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ps.95","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Psalms 95","reference":"Psalms 95","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"The author of this psalm was David, as is affirmed, Heb. iv, 7.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"It has a special reference to the days of the Messiah; as it is understood by the apostle, Heb. iii, 7, &c. and Heb. iv, 3-9.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"Herein we are called upon, to praise God, as a great and gracious God, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"1-7.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"To hear God's voice, and not harden our hearts, lest we fall as the Israelites did, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"8-11.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"3.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":8,"text":"God's - Above all that are called God's angels, earthly potentates, and especially the false gods of the Heathen.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":9,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":10,"text":"Hand - Under his government.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":11,"text":"Strength - The strongest or highest mountains.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":12,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":13,"text":"Pasture - Whom he feeds and keeps in his own pasture, or in the land which he hath appropriated to himself.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":14,"text":"The sheep - Which are under his special care.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":15,"text":"Today - Forthwith or presently.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":16,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":17,"text":"Harden not - By obstinate unbelief.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":18,"text":"Provocation - In that bold and wicked contest with God in the wilderness.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":19,"text":"Temptation - In the day in which you tempted me.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":20,"text":"9.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":21,"text":"Works - Both of mercy, and of justice.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":22,"text":"10.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":23,"text":"Do err - Their hearts are insincere and bent to backsliding.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":24,"text":"Not known - After all my teaching and discoveries of myself to them; they did not know, nor consider, those great things which I had wrought for them.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":25,"text":"11.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":26,"text":"My rest - Into the promised land, which is called the rest, Deut. xii, 9.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":95}}